## §1 What is under test

`spec/SAEOS-1-architecture.md` §9 A8 carries the specification's self-declared
**"single largest untested assumption"**:

> **A8** — "Ω1 (self-population) is presented as a breakthrough but assumes PAEOS
> emits clean structured decisions. Does it?" **[MODIFY]** Partially. PAEOS
> *produces* all the required artifacts (L06 matrices, L08 design sets, L11
> contracts, decision-graph records, scars), but as prose documents, not as typed
> emission bundles. Slice S1 (§8) exists precisely to build and test that
> extraction. **Carried:** if L15 artifacts prove too unstructured to extract
> losslessly, S1 fails and Ω1's value is overstated.

D7 (§10) ratified this risk "scoped: S1 is explicitly a falsification test." This
probe runs that test **by hand, before building S1**, against the corpus that
exists today.

The concrete claim being falsified is the §6.1b emission-bundle mapping:

```
Decision   ← from the decision-graph (ADR records + constitutional_basis)
TradeOff   ← from the L06 trade-off matrix
Option     ← from L04 candidates, INCLUDING rejected ones
Constraint ← from the L11 implementation contract
Component  ← from the L08 architecture artifact set
Scar       ← from the scar-graph (root-cause bundle, A-10)
EvidenceRef← hashes only; evidence never leaves PAEOS
```

## §2 Method

**Instrument.** For each goal, every field of the SAEOS-1 §4.2 universal envelope
(17 fields) plus every field of the seven §4.3 node types the §6.1b bundle emits
(26 fields) is scored against the goal's real sealed artifacts:

| Score | Meaning | Weight |
|---|---|---|
| **extractable** | The value is present in a sealed artifact and can be lifted directly, or is legitimately minted by the emitter (ids, timestamps, `status: candidate`). | 1.0 |
| **partial** | The information exists but must be inferred, compressed, or reconstructed by convention; or only some instances of the type carry it. | 0.5 |
| **absent** | No source exists in any sealed artifact. | 0.0 |

`loss_ratio = 1 − (Σ score / fields attempted)`. 43 fields per goal, 129 total.

**Type-specific field inventory (26):** Decision {choice_made, context,
alternatives_considered, rationale, constitutional_basis}; Option
{candidate_description, rejected_flag, rejection_reason}; Constraint {limit_kind,
limit_value, source}; TradeOff {axis, party_a, party_b, resolution}; Component
{name, kind, interfaces, dependencies}; Scar {root_cause, detection_signature,
guard_action}; EvidenceRef {hash, uri, kind, reverification_instructions}.

**Sample selection — declared bias.** The three goals below were chosen as
**best-case**, not representative: each has an unusually rich decision record (a
ratified Improvement Proposal or a founder-ratified debt entry). 13 of 42 sealed
goals have an IP; most have none. **The measured loss is therefore a floor.** A
random sample would score worse, and this is the strongest form the probe can
take: if the best cases fail the bar, the corpus fails it.

