| A-f | Prose is losslessly convertible to typed nodes by an extractor | A8 "[MODIFY] Partially" | **Not falsified, but not sufficient.** Prose→type conversion is not the binding constraint; *source absence* is. Better extraction cannot recover a field with no source. |
| A-g | This probe's own sample is representative | *this document* | **Explicitly denied** (§2). Sample is best-case-biased; 0.33 is a floor. |
| A-h | Field-equal weighting reflects consumer value | *this document* | **Carried, unresolved.** An unweighted mean under-penalises TradeOff/EvidenceRef relative to their S2 criticality — §5 compensates qualitatively rather than by re-weighting. A consumer-weighted instrument would score worse. |

### §6.2 Perspectives covered (L09 seven-stance sweep)

| Stance | Finding |
|---|---|
| **Builder** | Extractor is buildable today (markdown → typed nodes); the blocker is missing sources, not parsing difficulty. R1 is a one-line re-source. |
| **Architect** | §6.1b's source map is decoupled from PAEOS's real artifact topology in 3 of 7 lines. Fix the map, not the ontology — §4.3's twelve types are otherwise sound. |
| **Risk Officer** | Shipping S1 unmodified encodes two false specification claims (lossless scar round-trip; resolvable EvidenceRef) into a corpus that later consumers will trust. Cost of delay is one sprint; cost of the false claim compounds. |
| **Performance** | Not material at S1. Bundle sizes are ~4–7 KB/goal × 42 goals; the §5.1 token budget is untested here and out of probe scope. |
| **Security** | **Highest-severity finding (§4.4).** §3.3.3's "no evidence minting" is the guarantee that makes a poisoned SAKG harmless. An unresolvable `EvidenceRef` converts a structural guarantee into a policy promise — precisely the failure FPL-3 forbids. Blocks GO independently of the loss ratio. |
| **Replay** | `provenance.source_hash` (sha256 of the review file) is extractable, so extraction *is* reproducible — the one §5.1 `corpus_hash` prerequisite that already holds. |
| **Maintainer** | Prose review format is stable across all 42 files (identical H2 skeleton), so an extractor will not rot quickly. Sustainable if R1–R3 land. |

